Sound stage 5: the stream iOS plays into, /dev/redwood-audio (spescodec=4), after Topaz 0146.

all28 played the stage 3 tone out of the speaker. Stage 3's steps are split (s3_open / s3_run /
s3_ports / s3_rx2 / s3_write / s3_close; the tone test is unchanged), and spescodec=4 keeps the
stream open as Topaz's TopazAudio stream does, on spes's APR push path: /dev/redwood-audio (the
ABI of HackiOS's RedwoodAudio.driver, created at spes_audio_init so the plug-in finds it) fills a
1 s FIFO without waiting; the audio thread runs the session once, sets up the ports once, turns
RX2 on and keeps 6 periods with the DSP, refilled from the FIFO (silence where short) as they
come back; 0.5 s after the last write it mutes and turns RX2 off. Volume: RX2 digital gain,
spesvol dB (default -12) less iOS's attenuation.

